            <div xml:id="d1473">

                <pb facs="1169" n="1159" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1159"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.8571/5–2649: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-05-28T15:00:00-04:00">May 28, 1949—3 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1081. Asst. Secy Rusk discussed substance urtel 1840 May 26 with Amb Koo same day
                    quoting ur statement that “Nationalists have wantonly fired on Amer flag”. Rusk
                    told Koo Dept did not intend give publicity this matter but indicated Dept’s
                    deep concern over report. Koo stated wld immed wire Chi Govt, Canton, urging
                    cessation firing by Nationalists on US Govt property.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
